---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "support/index.html"
title: "CueCard Support - Get Help with the Teleprompter App"
description: "Support for CueCard Teleprompter. Email a person, report a bug on GitHub, ask for your account and data to be deleted, or read the answers to the questions we get most."
keywords: "cuecard support, teleprompter app support, cuecard help, cuecard contact, report a bug cuecard, cuecard account deletion, teleprompter app not working"
canonical: "https://cuecard.dev/support/"
pageName: "CueCard Support"
ogTitle: "CueCard Support - get help with the teleprompter"
ogDescription: "Email a person, report a bug, or ask us to delete your account. Every message is read."
ogLocale: "en_US"
crumbs:
  - name: "CueCard"
    url: "/"
  - name: "Support"
    url: "/support/"
---
{% block jsonld %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "ContactPage",
    "@id": "https://cuecard.dev/support/#contactpage",
    "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://cuecard.dev/#website" },
    "inLanguage": "en",
    "about": { "@id": "https://cuecard.dev/#org" },
    "mainEntity": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "@id": "https://cuecard.dev/#org",
        "contactPoint": [
            {
                "@type": "ContactPoint",
                "contactType": "customer support",
                "email": "{{ site.email }}",
                "url": "https://cuecard.dev/support/",
                "availableLanguage": "English"
            },
            {
                "@type": "ContactPoint",
                "contactType": "technical support",
                "url": "{{ site.issues }}",
                "availableLanguage": "English"
            }
        ]
    }
}
</script>
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}
{% include "partials/nav.njk" %}

<main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-h">
        <div class="wrap">
            {% include "partials/breadcrumbs.njk" %}
            <h1 class="display reveal" id="hero-h">Something not working? <em>Tell us.</em></h1>
            <p class="body reveal d1">
                CueCard is made by a very small team, which means the person who reads your
                email is the person who can fix the thing you are writing about. There is no
                ticket queue and no bot in front of it.
            </p>
            <div class="actions reveal d2">
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">
                    {{ icon("mail", 17) }}Email {{ site.email }}
                </a>
                <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{ site.issues }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    {{ icon("github", 17) }}Report a bug on GitHub
                </a>
            </div>
            <span class="meta-note reveal d2">Usually answered within a couple of days · English</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# The three ways in, and what each one is actually for. Sending a bug to
       the inbox and a billing question to the issue tracker both work, but the
       page may as well say which lands fastest. #}
    <section class="rows solid" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-h">
        <div class="wrap">
            <p class="micro">{{ icon("mail", 13) }}Ways to reach us</p>
            <h2 class="section-h" id="contact-h">Three doors, all of them open</h2>
            <ol class="rowlist">
                <li class="row reveal">
                    <span class="row-n">01</span>
                    <div class="row-body">
                        <h3>Email</h3>
                        <p>
                            <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> — for anything
                            at all: a question, a bug, a feature you wish existed, or a request to
                            delete your account. Tell us which device and which version you are on
                            and the first reply is far more likely to be the useful one.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="row reveal">
                    <span class="row-n">02</span>
                    <div class="row-body">
                        <h3>GitHub issues</h3>
                        <p>
                            CueCard is open source, so bugs and feature requests live in the open on
                            <a href="{{ site.issues }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the issue
                            tracker</a>. Filing there means you can watch the fix happen, and it
                            means the next person with the same problem finds your report.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="row reveal">
                    <span class="row-n">03</span>
                    <div class="row-body">
                        <h3>The FAQ</h3>
                        <p>
                            Most of what arrives in the inbox is already answered on
                            <a href="/faq/">the FAQ page</a> — the overlay permission on iOS, why
                            the notes stay invisible in a screen share, what CueCard costs. It is
                            searchable, and it is the fastest answer available at 2am.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# The questions that arrive as support mail rather than as curiosity. Each
       one is the short version; the FAQ page carries the long one. #}
    <section id="common" aria-labelledby="common-h">
        <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
            <p class="micro">{{ icon("help", 13) }}Before you write in</p>
            <h2 class="section-h" id="common-h">The five we answer most</h2>
            <div class="faq-list">
                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        <span>The prompter will not float over my other apps on iPhone</span>
                        {{ icon("chevron", 20, "faq-icon") }}
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            The floating window needs the Picture in Picture permission, and iOS only
                            offers it the first time you start the prompter. If you dismissed that
                            prompt, quit CueCard, reopen it and start a script again. You need
                            {{ site.requiresMobile }}. Still stuck? Write in and say which iPhone.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        <span>My notes showed up in the screen share on Zoom or Meet</span>
                        {{ icon("chevron", 20, "faq-icon") }}
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            Share a <em>window</em> or a <em>tab</em> rather than your entire screen.
                            Sharing the whole display shares everything on it, CueCard included —
                            that is the operating system doing what it was asked, not a bug.
                            <a href="/desktop/">How it works on the desktop app</a>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        <span>Delete my account and the data attached to it</span>
                        {{ icon("chevron", 20, "faq-icon") }}
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> from the
                            address you signed in with and we will remove it. Your scripts live on
                            your own device and go with the app when you uninstall it. What we hold
                            and why is set out in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        <span>Google Slides notes are not reaching the desktop app</span>
                        {{ icon("chevron", 20, "faq-icon") }}
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            The sync needs both halves: the desktop app open, and the browser
                            extension installed in the browser you are presenting from. Both are
                            on <a href="/google-slides/">the Google Slides page</a>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        <span>When is Android coming?</span>
                        {{ icon("chevron", 20, "faq-icon") }}
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            It is being built, and it is not out yet — we do not have a date to give
                            you, and we would rather say so than invent one.
                            <a href="/mobile/android/">The Android page</a> is where it will be
                            announced.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>
            </div>
            <p class="backline">
                <a href="/faq/">{{ icon("help", 15) }} Every question, answered {{ icon("arrow", 14) }}</a>
                <a href="/privacy/">{{ icon("shield", 15) }} Privacy policy {{ icon("arrow", 14) }}</a>
                <a href="/terms/">{{ icon("book", 15) }} Terms of service {{ icon("arrow", 14) }}</a>
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    {% set ctaHeading = "Still stuck?<br /><em>Just ask.</em>" %}
    {% set ctaBody = 'Email <a href="mailto:' + site.email + '">' + site.email + '</a> or open an issue on GitHub. Both are read by a person.' %}
    {% set ctaPrimaryHref = "mailto:" + site.email %}
    {% set ctaPrimaryIcon = "mail" %}
    {% set ctaPrimaryText = "Email support" %}
    {% set ctaSecondaryHref = site.issues %}
    {% set ctaSecondaryIcon = "github" %}
    {% set ctaSecondaryText = "Open an issue" %}
    {% set ctaNote = "Free · Open source · MIT licensed" %}
    {% include "partials/cta.njk" %}
</main>

{% include "partials/footer.njk" %}
{% endblock %}
